  "text": "A plot often can't be handed over until its paperwork is complete, and waiting for documents is often what holds a handover up. KeyCheck tracks the paperwork so you can see what's missing and how long you've been waiting. Each document is marked as one of these: Received : you have it. Outstanding : you've asked for it and are waiting. Not checked : nobody has looked at it yet. Not applicable : it doesn't apply to this plot. KeyCheck saves the date every time a document's status changes. So without any extra typing, you can see that a certificate has been \"Waiting 12 days · chased yesterday\", or prove when it arrived. This works for: Plot documents , which each plot needs its own copy of, such as EPCs, gas safety certificates and electrical certificates Project documents , which the site needs once, such as the fire strategy or warranties Bundles , for requirements made up of several separate items, such as a set of collateral warranties Planning conditions , which KeyCheck can read from a council's decision notice and sort into conditions needed before work starts, before occupation, or ongoing From the office Documents can be updated one plot at a time on site, or for many plots at once from the office. For example, if the EPCs for plots 12 to 20 arrive in one email, you can mark them all as received in one go. Chapter 6 covers document tracking in detail. Needs attention , on the Site tab, lists what to act on: documents nobody has chased for a while, final snags that are overdue, and plots past or near their target handover date. KeyCheck can remind you with a notification, and there's a Needs attention widget for the Home Screen and Lock Screen. Chapter 9 explains more."
